arxiv-2105-14646.description:
A 2021 arXiv research paper by martina liccardo *. We investigate the property of elimination of imaginaries for some special cases of ordered abelian groups. We show that certain Hahn products of ordered abelian groups do not eliminate imaginaries in the pure language of ordered groups. Moreover, we prove that, adding finitely many constants to the language of ordered abelian groups, the theories of the finite lexicographic products
\mathbb{Z}^{n}
and
\mathbb{Z}^{n}\times\mathbb{Q}
have definable Skolem functions. Introduction

Proving elimination of imaginaries is essentially a definability problem.
